their preference by using *e.* instead of *show.*
>>>

<<<
Right use: This work of Mr Phillipps, while it bears all the marks of scholarship, bears also the far rarer impress of original thought, & evidences the power of considering with an unusual detachment a subject which ..
===
Right use: *This work of Mr Phillipps, while it bears all the marks of scholarship, bears also the far rarer impress of original thought, & evidences the power of considering with an unusual detachment a subject which* . . .
>>>

<<<
Wrong use: Mr Thayer evidences a remarkable grasp of his material, & a real gift for the writing of history.
===
Wrong use: *Mr Thayer evidences a remarkable grasp of his material, & a real gift for the writing of history.*
>>>

<<<
Negative use: We regret that his work should be so unambitious in scope, for it fails to include many of the popular superstitions of today, does not evidence any great care or research in its composition, & its arrangement is amateurish.
===
Negative use: *We regret that his work should be so unambitious in scope, for it fails to include many of the popular superstitions of today, does not evidence any great care or research in its composition, & its arrangement is amateurish.*
>>>

